You must have the "Piper PA28-161 Warrior II" already installed. 

  You may find her on "FGHangar". 
  In order to use FGHangar, just go to the "Add-on" section on the Startup screen and check the "Flightgear aircraft Distribution" option for your Flightgear version (2020.x or 2024.x at the moment of writing).

If you already have the original "Piper PA-28 Warrior II installed, you just copy and paste the "PA28" folder inside your Aicraft directory; just replace the original files with the new ones.

For example, if you want to use the Terminal on Debian/Ubuntu Linux with Flightgear 2024.x you may use these commands:

cd /tmp ;
git clone https://github.com/ubuntuperonista/piper-warrior/ ;
cd /tmp/piper-warrior/ ;
mv Aircraft/PA28 /home/$USER/.fgfs/Aircraft/org.flightgear.fgaddon.stable_2024/
